paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part01.tex:9:The twenty-three stages here should be read as a single construction.  Stage~001 promotes the old collective geometry variables to a distributed moving-surface field and introduces the scalar, grouped real \(P_2\), and higher-harmonic lanes.  Stage~002 verifies that this distributed wall theory reduces back to the old \((a,L)\) closure in the lowest axisymmetric sector.  Stage~003 couples the wall to stable BdG matter support modes and derives the first conservative Schur-complement kernels.  Stages~004--021 now treat the electromagnetic sector projection-first: they derive the exact projected localized Maxwell law, identify the matched zero-mode reduction, transport mouth-local projected corrections into the grouped \(Z_n,N_n\) slots, import the parent-throat action packet, and retain the previous Maxwell/mixed one-port calculation as the reduced normal form for outgoing transfer.  Stage~022 translates that outgoing bridge into the normalized grouped-response language used by the retarded quadrupole program.  Stage~023 writes the full grouped \(20/21/22\) bundle, its weighted projectors, its microscopic coefficient ledger, and the isotropic normalization test.
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part01.tex:73:The derivations below preserve the status distinction used throughout the ledger.  Algebraic eliminations, projector identities, low-frequency expansions, and grouped inverse maps are exact once the declared reduced variables are adopted.  The projection-first Maxwell law is exact after the observation kernel is declared; the matched zero-mode and one-port Maxwell/mixed normal forms are controlled reductions.  The adoption of a distributed wall closure, a stable BdG normal-mode reduction, and a compact outgoing port are reduced or effective moves.  The final equality of the outgoing-normalization product with the universal quadrupole target is not proved in this appendix; it is formulated here as the branch test that later stages attempt to realize.
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part01.tex:128:\section{Part I appendix closure and handoff to Part II}
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part01.tex:129:\label{sec:app-part01-closure}
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:63:166 & Bundle inversion of the last four drifts & \StatusExactClosure{} & Inverts the four observables \((\Theta_w,K_s,K_q,P_0)\) to determine the four remaining microscopic drifts. \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:95:182 & Microscopic coherent-kernel slippages & \StatusExactClosure{} & Reduces the defect to \((\Sigma_Z,\Sigma_\chi,\Sigma_\epsilon,\Sigma_\delta)\) plus dressing slippage \(\Sigma_\eta\), and isolates \(\Sigma_{\rm tr}\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:97:183 & Triangular normal form & \StatusExactClosure{} & Compresses the coherent weak-axisymmetric problem to \((\Sigma_{\rm tr},\Sigma_{\rm nt},\Sigma_\eta)\) with triangular map to \((\Theta_1,\Xi_1,\mathcal R_1)\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:105:187 & Orbit--quotient closure & \StatusExactClosure{} & Proves finite level sets of \((\mathfrak C_{{\rm tr},*},\mathfrak C_{{\rm nt},*},\epsilon_\eta)\) are exactly \(\mathcal G_*\)-orbits. \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:107:188 & Branch-observable compiler & \StatusExactClosure{} & Compiles direct branch observables to \((\Theta_1,\Xi_1,\mathcal R_1)\) and records equivalent observable packets. \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:121:195 & Source-map reduction & \StatusExactClosure{} / \StatusReduced{} & Factorizes the observable odd closure as \(\widehat m_0^{2}\chi_QN_Q=1\) and collapses \(\Delta_{\rm norm}\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:125:197 & Conditional Packet-A closure & \StatusExactClosure{} & Proves \(\Delta_{\rm branch}=0\iff \chi_Q=1\) and hence \(\Delta_Q=\chi_Q-1\) is the sole Packet-A scalar. \\
paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:135:\claimstatus{Mixed but predominantly \StatusExactClosure{}.  Stages 164--200 are exact algebra inside the declared co-evolving Family--1, grouped real \(P_2\), coherent local D/N, outgoing-prefactor, Packet-A, and Packet-B reduced hierarchies.  The natural point-particle source-map use in Stage 195 is a \StatusReduced{} import.  The actual nonlinear moving-throat PDE still has to return branch data that land on the final packet; realization by that branch remains \StatusOpen{} even though the compilers and quotient/orbit theorems are exact within closure.}
